## 2. The system we should design

I recommend a multi-university platform with institution-specific integrations.

The core system remains shared. Each university gets its own configuration, authorized staff, student population, branding, academic rules, and integration adapter.

Student experience

Digital ID · QR · Status · Renewal

Authenticated platform APIs

AstraMind Digital ID Core

Credential issuance · Verification · Payments · Revocation · Audit

LUANAR adapter

Registry / SIS connection

Other university adapters

Institution-specific connections

University systems of record

Student registration · Enrollment status · Programme · Academic records

Conceptual architecture, not a claim that any named university has already provided an API or agreed to integrate.

### Why this architecture matters

If LUANAR uses an API, we build an API connector. If another university has a different system, we build a different connector. If access is initially limited to approved data exports, we can develop a controlled import workflow.

The central platform should not need to be rewritten each time a university joins.

Each university must also be isolated from the others. A LUANAR administrator must never be able to view or change KUHeS student records, for example.

